# Venus Reviews - Hostinger .htaccess
RewriteEngine On
DirectoryIndex index.html
Options -Indexes

# Clean URLs - add .html extension for existing files only
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_FILENAME} !-f
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_FILENAME} !-d
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_FILENAME}.html -f
RewriteRule ^(.*)$ $1.html [L]

# Custom error pages
ErrorDocument 404 /404.html
ErrorDocument 500 /500.html

# Redirect old WordPress-style URLs to new structure
Redirect 301 /privacy-policy/ /privacy/
Redirect 301 /reviews/ /products/
Redirect 301 /blog/ /guides/
Redirect 301 /category/vibrators/ /products/
Redirect 301 /category/dildos/ /products/

# Retired duplicate/stale product pages (removed 2026-07-30 when best-of shipped).
# None were in the sitemap, but redirect rather than 404 in case of stray links.
# 2026-08-25: bvee-original-rabbit and womanizer-2-original removed AGAIN. Both are
# fabricated products (no such manufacturer / no such SKU) retired by the 2026-08-06
# content-integrity pass; the 2026-08-08 best-of promotion (324591c) reintroduced
# them and they were undrafted 2026-08-17. Their URLs were live and in the sitemap,
# so 301 rather than 404. Do not re-add these pages without a manufacturer source.
Redirect 301 /products/bvee-original-rabbit/ /products/
Redirect 301 /products/womanizer-2-original/ /products/
Redirect 301 /products/bvee-rabbit/ /products/
Redirect 301 /products/womanizer-2/ /products/
Redirect 301 /products/h2o-holo-vibe/ /products/
Redirect 301 /products/all/ /products/

# "H2O Holo Vibe" was never a real product. The retired page described a
# "holographic display" device that does not exist from any manufacturer, so
# there is nothing to point a reader at beyond the catalogue index.
Redirect 301 /products/h2o-holo-vibe/ /products/

# Retired 2026-08-05: lelo-gigi-2, satisfyer-pro-2 and womanizer-premium-2 used to
# redirect here because no review existed. Real sourced reviews now live at those
# URLs, so the redirects are gone - a Redirect directive wins over the filesystem
# and would have masked the new pages.

# Superseded Best For pages (removed 2026-08-05). These were unlinked, absent from
# the sitemap, and duplicated the indexed pages they now point to.
# 2026-08-17: slug changed from 'best-for-couples'/'best-for-travel' to 'couples'/'travel',
# so the clean URLs now serve the real content. The redirects to the old slug-based URLs
# are removed so filesystem content takes precedence.
Redirect 301 /products/compare/ /products/

# Retired tag pages (removed 2026-08-06). Orphaned build artifacts: the product pages
# that carried these tags lost their `tags:` front matter in the 2026-07-30 best-of
# rewrite, so `hugo` stopped emitting the listings, but the already-built directories
# stayed committed. They were served for roughly two weeks in July, so redirect rather
# than 404.
#
# Corrected 2026-08-06: an earlier version of this comment claimed none were in the
# sitemap and nothing linked to them. Both were wrong - four (compact, external,
# g-spot, waterproof) were in sitemap.xml, and nine dead tag links were still listed
# in tags/index.html, 404.html and tags/index.xml. All were cleaned up in 8b8c7c1.
# It also said "the ten tags still in use"; there are six.
#
# VERSION BRANCH: compact, external, g-spot and waterproof are un-retired here -
# they are real product facets still declared by 3 products. The names below are
# listed explicitly so the live tags cannot match:
#   air-pulse  ergonomic  premium  quiet  swedish-design  value
# Before editing this rule, re-derive that list - it is the directories under tags/,
# and it must equal the /tags/ entries in sitemap.xml.
#
# 2026-08-25: added airpulse, beginner-friendly, dual-stimulation,
# intelligent-sensitivity and rabbit - orphaned when the fabricated
# bvee-original-rabbit and womanizer-2-original products (their only members)
# were removed again. They were live and in the sitemap, so redirect rather
# than 404.
RedirectMatch 301 ^/tags/(adjustable|airpulse|app-control|app-controlled|beginner-friendly|couples|dual-action|dual-motors|dual-stimulation|exploratory|external-stimulator|german-engineering|intelligent-sensitivity|medical-grade|mens-health|personal-massager|precision|pressure-wave|prostate|rabbit|rechargeable|sonic|specialized|synchronized|travel-friendly|twin-tip|wellness|whisper-quiet|wraparound)/?$ /products/

# --- Source & tooling exposure fix (2026-07-31) ---
# The hostinger-deploy branch holds the Hugo SOURCE alongside the served output, and
# Hostinger serves the branch root, so everything was publicly fetchable: 134 .md
# (including every page's raw markdown, duplicating the rendered HTML), 20 .sh, 12 .py,
# hugo.toml, and internal planning docs. No credentials were exposed, but the raw
# markdown is a genuine duplicate-content problem and the rest is simply not public
# business.

# Block source, tooling and planning file types at the root level.
# json added 2026-08-25: affiliate-config.json and affiliate-credentials-template.json
# (internal affiliate-program planning, incl. program statuses) plus badge-prompts.json
# and comfy-prompts.json (image-gen tooling) were publicly readable. The site serves no
# legitimate JSON - no search index, no manifest, no JS fetch of .json anywhere in the
# built output (verified 2026-08-25). If a manifest or /index.json is ever added, grant
# it explicitly like the convention .txt files below.
<FilesMatch "\.(md|sh|py|toml|yaml|yml|lock|bak|log|txt|json)$">
  Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

# Convention files must stay reachable despite the .txt rule above.
# ads.txt matters for an affiliate/ad site; keep it allowed now so adding one later
# does not silently 403.
<FilesMatch "^(robots|ads|app-ads|security|llms)\.txt$">
  Require all granted
</FilesMatch>

# Block source and tooling directories outright.
#
# public/ is Hugo's build output directory. deploy.sh rsyncs it to the branch root
# (what Hostinger serves), so every page under /public/ was a served duplicate of its
# root twin - confirmed 2026-08-05, /public/products/lelo-mona/ and /public/index.html
# both returned 200. Nothing links to /public/, and no page emits rel=canonical, so
# Google had two equally-valid copies of the whole site and no tiebreak. The copies had
# also drifted: /public/best-for/ was missing the five hand-written pages (couples,
# luxury, technology, travel, value) while still serving four retired ones.
# Also untracked from git in this same commit; this rule is the belt to that braces,
# since a Hostinger sync that does not delete would otherwise leave the files served.
RedirectMatch 404 ^/(content|layouts|archive|scripts|docs|data|public|credentials|\.claude|\.bin|\.backup)(/|$)

# 2026-08-25: the root-level planning .md files, internal .json configs, legacy
# tooling scripts, archive/, credentials/, affiliate-research/, docs/, .claude/
# and .backup/ were REMOVED from this branch entirely (archived to
# ~/.openclaw/workspaces/worker/venus-internal; the active ops scripts deploy.sh
# and visual-monitor-cronjob.sh moved to ~/.openclaw/scripts/venus/). The
# FilesMatch and directory rules above STAY: they still cover the Hugo source
# that must remain on this branch (content/*.md, hugo.toml, config/), and they
# keep any stale copies unreachable if Hostinger's sync ever fails to delete
# removed files (see the public/ note above - sync-without-delete is a known
# risk). credentials/ and .claude/ are in the blocked list for the same
# stale-copy reason even though they no longer exist on the branch.

# Trigger redeploy 2026-08-17 17:38 CEST
